description:
Design your own swirly star lantern to celebrate Matariki. This lantern may not help you find your way in the dark but it will remind you to look up at the beauty of the night sky.
Children must be supervised by a parent or guardian at all times.&nbsp;
No booking required - just drop in to the Auckland Botanic Gardens Visitor Centre and play!

Join Whimsy &amp; Co. Studio in a hands-on workshop where tamariki will create their own shimmering, story-filled planisphere inspired by Matariki.&nbsp;
They will be led through imaginative prompts to transform memories and dreams into stars, symbols and tiny visual worlds. Using a mix of materials, they will construct and decorate a rotating star wheel, layering on colour, texture and details to evoke their stories. The workshop will emphasise artistic freedom, abstract thinking and personal voice.
Each child will leave with a magical artwork - a small constellation of their own past, present and possibilities to come. For ages 5–12.

This production comes directly from her critically acclaimed solo performances of Shakespeare’s HAMLET, which were triple-extended in New York, Chicago, and London.
Nominated for New York’s: Drama League’s Distinguished Performance Award and Outer Critic’s Circle Outstanding Solo Performance Award.&nbsp;

“An impressive sweeping performance." ★★★★ – The Telegraph
“When it gets to the famous soliloquies, Izzard…smashes all three of the great ones.” ★★★★ – The Chicago Tribune
“Eddie Izzard’s Hamlet is spectacular.” – Dame Judi Dench&nbsp;

Akin to the original performances of HAMLET, Eddie will perform on the blank canvas of a bare stage, letting Shakespeare’s words and pure storytelling take the spotlight.
